WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.200
Speaker 1: So earlier in the show, we talked about&nbsp;
the hearings that took place yesterday, primarily&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:13.440
about the January 6th Trump riots, and we spoke&nbsp;
about Merrick Garland and other Biden officials&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:20.320
explaining in very clear terms white supremacists&nbsp;
are the top domestic terror threat. That wasn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:24.320
really the main focus of these hearings. The&nbsp;
main focus of these hearings was actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:28.880
what on earth happened on January 6th. And one&nbsp;
of the big questions about January 6th has been,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:36.560
did Trump get asked to deploy the National&nbsp;
Guard early and refused? Did Donald Trump not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:43.840
think about it? What exactly explained the delay&nbsp;
where we were still watching in the 4:00 p.m.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:50.080
Eastern hour and there were no National Guard and&nbsp;
the riots had been going on for hours. Protesters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:55.200
and rioters and insurrectionists had breached&nbsp;
the Capitol building. People had already died,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.200 --> 00:01:01.440
et cetera, et cetera. Well, yesterday, during&nbsp;
testimony and this is just unbelievable, Trump's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:09.360
former acting secretary of defense confirmed that&nbsp;
Donald Trump did not approve the plan to deploy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:16.960
the National Guard until Mike Pence called him&nbsp;
more than three hours after the capital riot began&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:26.480
yesterday. This was the testimony from Chris&nbsp;
Miller. Chris Miller was Trump's acting defense&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:33.520
secretary for that last period of the Trump&nbsp;
administration. And he said that it was a more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:40.960
than three hour delay from when the capital riot&nbsp;
started, to when Donald Trump actually authorized&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:46.080
the National Guard to go in. And of course, we&nbsp;
know that it took a while for the National Guard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:51.280
to actually get on site. It was already starting&nbsp;
to really become evening when that really took&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:57.360
place. And it took a phone call from Mike Pence&nbsp;
convincing him to do it before he was actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:04.160
willing to sign off on that. At first, former&nbsp;
acting defense secretary Chris Miller testified&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:10.960
that he gave full authorization to deploy members&nbsp;
of the National Guard at 3:00 p.m., which was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:15.440
about two hours, remember, right around 1:00 p.m.&nbsp;
Eastern. We were all watching it live. We were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:22.000
streaming live about 1:00 p.m. is when the breach&nbsp;
started. Three p.m. is initially what Chris Miller&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:29.280
said was the timing. Miller was then questioned by&nbsp;
New York Congresswoman Alexandria Cassio Cortez,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:35.440
and she started going more specifically&nbsp;
into the timeline of January 6th. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:40.240
then we eventually learned that actually&nbsp;
the National Guard was not authorized&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:47.840
to go to the Capitol until four thirty&nbsp;
two p.m. Eastern Time. And the delay,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:56.480
it's a little nebulous what the delay even was&nbsp;
part of it was coming up with a plan for exactly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.480 --> 00:03:00.640
how it would be done and so on and so&nbsp;
forth. But what's really interesting is that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:09.280
the the testimony revealed a conversation between&nbsp;
Miller and Mike Pence at 4:00 eight p.m. and AOC&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:16.000
asked, did Pence direct you to clear the building?&nbsp;
And Miller said, Well, I had a very brief&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:23.920
conversation with Mike Pence where we we agreed&nbsp;
that the building would be cleared, but the order&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:31.760
to actually do it was not issued until later after&nbsp;
a conversation with the mayor of Washington, D.C.,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:36.400
after a conversation with Speaker Nancy Pelosi,&nbsp;
after a conversation with Senate. At the time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:44.960
it was Senate Minority Leader Chuck Schumer.&nbsp;
And it was three hours after the mayor of D.C.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:50.480
actually asked for that deployment. So there&nbsp;
are really a couple of possibilities here.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:55.840
Neither of them is particularly good. And I would&nbsp;
kind of summarize them as either incompetence or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.400 --> 00:04:04.640
what some some might call treason, others might&nbsp;
call indifference. I don't know. One possibility&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:11.200
is Trump and his executive branch realize&nbsp;
the danger of what was going on right away.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:17.680
They understood the urgency of getting the&nbsp;
National Guard in quickly, but it took them three&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:22.800
and a half hours to do it because they were either&nbsp;
inept or they couldn't figure out how to do it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:28.320
or they were slow or whatever. So that makes them&nbsp;
weak. That makes them incompetent. That makes them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:32.720
everything that they showed us they are during&nbsp;
the Trump administration. That's one possibility.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:40.240
The second possibility is, in a sense, maybe even&nbsp;
worse, which is that Trump knew exactly what was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:45.360
going on on January 6th, starting at 1:00 p.m. and&nbsp;
we believe that he did because we are aware of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:51.360
fact that he was everybody at the White House was&nbsp;
watching what was going on up and that he chose to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:57.920
delay or not to send National Guard to the Capitol&nbsp;
because of the political orientation of the people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.920 --> 00:05:04.480
who were writing, which were Trump's. Supporters&nbsp;
and of course, that unfortunately seems to me the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:08.720
more likely explanation and the reason I say that&nbsp;
is we know that Donald Trump and everybody at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:13.360
White House were watching what was going on. We&nbsp;
have reports that Trump was increasingly getting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:22.160
agitated and annoyed that the rioters looked low&nbsp;
class. And as Trump supporters made Donald Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:27.440
look bad, which is absolutely something you only&nbsp;
say if you have an understanding of what it is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:33.920
that is going on. And so if you ask me, was this&nbsp;
incompetence or was this a malicious attitude, I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:39.760
probably lean towards the malicious attitude based&nbsp;
on everything I know. If you are coming away with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:46.160
this, from this with a different perspective, let&nbsp;
me know. But every time we learn something new,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:53.440
every time there's a new revelation, it points not&nbsp;
only to incompetence by the Trump administration.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.440 --> 00:06:00.240
Yes, there was plenty of incompetence, but&nbsp;
it points to an uncaring, malicious and in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:05.840
some cases borderline treasonous perspective&nbsp;
to what was going on that day on January 6th.

